# Role layer: wireless networking (client).
#
# A role layer is an ADDITIONAL intention list, composed on top of a
# minimal or product profile. Roles are profile data, not
# meta-packages: the package manager still owns the closure and no new
# package name is invented for a role.
#
# Scope: wireless client operation - scanning, regulatory compliance
# and open-network association. WPA/WPA2 association needs an
# associator, which this role deliberately does NOT pull in:
# wpa_supplicant (dual-init wpa_supplicant@.service plus OpenRC
# init script, unix-socket control, no D-Bus) is the supported one -
# add it explicitly on machines that join protected networks. iwd is
# not packaged. wireless-tools is legacy and stays optional (iw
# covers modern nl80211). hostapd belongs to a separate access-point
# capability, never to generic client networking.
#
# Firmware is hardware-selected, never universal: wireless-tools or
# full firmware families are per-machine additions for known
# hardware, not base intentions.
#
#   wireless-regdb   regulatory database: without it the kernel logs
#                    a regulatory.db load failure and stays on the
#                    world roaming domain (proven Minimer 2026-11-08).
#   iw               nl80211 configuration and scanning.
wireless-regdb
iw
